    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A league of 39 sovereign German states and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free cities</a> created at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagsatzung">Diet</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> under Austrian presidency.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klemens-von-metternich">Metternich</a> it repressed liberal and national movements through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlsbad-decrees">Carlsbad Decrees</a> of 1819 and later measures.</li><li>Rivalry between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> paralysed it, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866 ended it and opened the way to a Prussian-led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The black, red and gold flag of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> was first adopted officially in 1848 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-convention-german-confederation">Federal Diet of the German Confederation</a>, the body nationalists regarded as the symbol of reaction.</p></aside>
    </section>

